      "description" : {
         "content" : [
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "Possibly lose Optional<> altogether. After C++ 17 - the case is less strong for the class.",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "But there are still several advantages, so maybe keep.",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "But at any rate - make it easy to convert both ways. From optional<> is easy. To optional maybe use As<> or something similar. Maybe .optional or .asoptional? - something easy to type/use. Whatever I do here - consider doing likewise for String (.aswstring) or .wstring).",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            }
         ],
         "type" : "doc",
         "version" : 1
      },
